#X text 678 51 Chord Generator;
#X text 51 98 I have added some functionality to vary the voicings. I always put the base note one octave down and leave the 7th where it is. For the 3rd \, I take it one octave up if it's 0.2 times above the base frequency. For the 5th \, I give it a 60% probability of going down an octave. I do this because I trunctuate the notes within an octave above the base note \, so that the chords stay in the same range \, and don't just keep rising as the scale degree increases. This makes it a bit stuffy. I want to add to this functionality \, but I don't have time.;
#X text 515 97 This subpatch takes in a scale degree and then makes the corresponding 7th chord relative to the key and passes it to the outlet as a sound object. The key and scale is sent through the sends 'key' and 'scale' from the parent patch. In this exact pd project \, they come from the subpatch [key-scale]., f 70;
#X text 45 296 7th chord: 1 - 3 - 5 - 7 --> Scale degree + 0 - 2 - 4 - 6 -->, f 62;
